content:
Implemented (this session, alongside #23). Extended the mod-tree directive emission to add a #[path = ...] attribute when a non-leaf NSID segment differs from its snake-case form (e.g. bad-example → bad_example).

Code change in proto-blue-codegen/src/generator.rs::Generator::generate(), PASS 3 mod.rs emission:

Before: leaf children with snake != child got #[path = \"<child>.rs\"]; non-leaf segments with the same mismatch got plain pub mod <snake>; (and rustc couldn't find <snake>/mod.rs because the directory on disk was at <child>/).

After: BOTH leaf and non-leaf cases get #[path] when the disk-path differs from the rust-ident form:
  if needs_path_attr {
      let suffix = if is_leaf { \".rs\" } else { \"/mod.rs\" };
      mod_content.push_str(&format!(\"#[path = \\\"{child}{suffix}\\\"]\\npub mod {rust_ident};\\n\"));
  } else {
      mod_content.push_str(&format!(\"pub mod {rust_ident};\\n\"));
  }

For com.bad-example.* this now emits at the com/mod.rs level:
  #[path = \"bad-example/mod.rs\"]
  pub mod bad_example;

The existing camelCase leaf case (e.g. getSession) is unchanged — that branch already worked, and my code preserves it (suffix = \".rs\" when is_leaf).

Verification (rust-quality §honest reporting):
  cargo test -p proto-blue-codegen                                  PASS (19 tests)
  cargo build --workspace                                           PASS
  cargo test --workspace                                            PASS (67 suites, 0 failures)
  cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings             PASS
  cargo fmt --all --check                                           PASS

Wild-corpus rustc-compile pass against the 420-doc slice that originally surfaced this bug: the E0583 cannot find file for module bad_example error is GONE. com.bad-example.identity.resolveMiniDoc and com.bad-example.repo.getUriRecord now resolve correctly via the #[path] attribute on com/mod.rs.

Behavioural change: same regen as #23 (229 files); the new #[path] attribute appears on any non-leaf segment whose snake-case form differs from the original NSID segment. The bundled bsky/atproto/chat/tools corpus contains no dash-bearing NSIDs, so the bundled regen output is unchanged.

Category: A (root-cause) — fixed the path-vs-ident invariant uniformly across the leaf and non-leaf cases of the mod-tree directive emission.
